# Build context is the repository root; keep everything generated, local or
# secret out of the image.
**/node_modules
**/.git
**/.next
**/build
**/coverage
**/dist
**/out
**/data
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.test.example
**/.claude
**/CLAUDE.md
**/AGENTS.md
*.pre-monorepo

# The runtime stage copies whole workspaces, so anything not excluded here ships
# to production. Prose first:
**/reports
**/docs
**/TODO.md
**/i18n-db.txt
**/prompt*.md
# The back end reads no Markdown; the front end serves some from `public/`.
apps/back-end/**/*.md

# Then the test suite — the largest thing in the back-end and served by nothing.
#
# `tsconfig.json` includes `**/*.ts`, so the `verify` stage's `bun check`
# would type-check these too; the image needs only what it ships to check, and
# CI's `bun run lint` type-checks the suite on every push regardless. Nothing
# outside `tests/` may import from it, or the verify stage's `bun run build`
# fails on a missing module.
**/tests
